<title>GERMANY: TABLE - West German June ind. orders rise 1.7 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE - West German June ind. orders rise 1.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS    June 97     May 97     June 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)   +1.7	 -1.5	  +1.4</p>
<p> Year-on-year			+5.2	 +4.8	  +1.2</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		101.4	 99.7	  96.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted, provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details (mth-on-mth)</p>
<p>				   June 97   May 97   June 97 index</p>
<p> Domestic orders		+1.8     -1.9	89.8</p>
<p> Foreign orders		 +1.4     -1.1     124.4</p>
<p> Intermediate goods	   +1.2     +0.6     104.9</p>
<p> Capital goods		  +1.5     -2.9     101.4</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables   +3.7     -4.6	92.8</p>
<p>Two-month comparison May/June 97 with Mar/Apr 97:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		    +1.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison May/June 97 with May/June 96:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		    +5.2</p>
<p> Domestic orders			+0.7</p>
<p> Foreign orders			+12.4</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		   +9.2</p>
<p> Capital goods			  +1.4</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	   +2.2</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
